ts\n    42\t   laid out as the parameters are written. `py/call-kw` (and `py/call`,\n    43\t   its positional-only form) binds positional arguments, keywords, defaults,\n    44\t   `*args` and `**kwargs` from the function's static spec; every binding\n    45\t   failure is a Python TypeError.\n    46\t\n    47\t   Runtime state is two cells, reached through the store (`yin/def` is\n    48\t   reserved for the prelude and builtins):\n    49\t     py.rt/handlers  the handler stack: frames [kind payload rest depth];\n    50\t                     a :handler frame holds the continuation `raise`\n    51\t                     delivers to, a :finally frame a thunk every exit\n    52\t                     through it runs (raise passes the exception, escapes\n    53\t                     and normal completion pass None), a :generator frame\n    54\t                     the bottom of a running generator's own stack (raise\n    55\t                     passes it the exception); nil when empty\n    56\t     py.rt/out       the values `print` collected, one vector per call\n    57\t\n    58\t   Escapes and handlers tell the first pass through a capture point from a\n    59\t   re-entry with a flag cell allocated before the capture (`:first`, then\n    60\t   `:re-entered`): heap writes survive continuation invocation, so the flag\n    61\t   answers without inspecting the continuation's representation. An escape\n    62\t   unwinds to the depth it captured, running finally thunks on the way.\n    63\t\n    64\t   Integer `//`, `%`, `**`, bitwise operators and float floor have no\n    65\t   portable host primitive; they are exact algorithms here over + - * <\n    66\t   (doubling division, binary-descent floor, two's-complement recursion),\n    67\t   valid within 2^53.\n    68\t\n    69\t   Host names the prelude depends on and does not define: `host-names`\n    70\t   (the cell module from yin.vm.module, the rest from yin.vm.data).\"\n    71\t  (:require\n    72\t    [yang.pyt